# the LCD-2 build (this fork: the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-2): on top of sdkconfig.defaults
#   idf.py -B <dir> -DSDKCONFIG=<dir>/sdkconfig -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.tlcd2" build
# (tools/build_tlcd2.sh). ESP32-S3R8 - 16 MB flash and 8 MB octal PSRAM, as the 1.8 -
# with a 2" ST7789T3 IPS (240 x 320, scanned landscape 320 x 240), a CST816D touch
# panel and a QMI8658 IMU. No codec, no PMIC, no RTC chip: the audio port is the
# stub, the battery meter stays hidden (no AXP2101 answers) and the clock is the
# system time kept through deep sleep. The tank is the rectangle's 448x368 world,
# scaled down to the glass by the display port.
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_TLCD2=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_SH8601=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_QVGA_SPI=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_TOUCH_FT3168=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_AUDIO_ES8311=n
# The onboard QMI8658 senses handling (the tank light) but does not turn the
# picture: its axes on this board are not measured (with the 1.8's it flipped
# back and forth in the hand). To have the IMU turn it, measure them (hold it
# right side up, run the director's `imu`), set them for this board in
# imu_port_qmi8658.c, and turn CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_AUTO_FLIP back on.
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_MPU6050=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_AUTO_FLIP=n
